+> **1.0.1 fixes inverted steering.** In 1.0 every steering control was
+> mirrored: A/left went right and D/right went left, on the keyboard, both
+> sticks and the tilt. The cause was a sign convention: the chase camera's
+> right-hand axis is `cross(forward, up) = (-sin h, 0, cos h)`, which is
+> the same vector as the simulation's lateral basis, so increasing the
+> heading turns the car toward the *right* of the screen — the opposite of
+> what the code's comments claimed. The physics and the AI were
+> self-consistent; only the human input mapping was backwards. Steering
+> polarity now lives in one place (`STEER_LEFT` / `STEER_RIGHT` in
+> `source/game.h`) and a test re-derives the camera axis to prove a left
+> input moves the car left across the screen.
+
 | Action      | USB keyboard | GameCube pad (Xbox in Dolphin) | Wii Remote (sideways) | + Nunchuk | Classic |
 |-------------|--------------|--------------------------------|------------------------|-----------|---------|
 | Steer left / right | **A** / **D** (or ← / →) | Main stick | Tilt or D-pad | Stick | Left stick |
